# Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL suppressions for the docker workflow's image scan.
# Mirrors the backend pip-audit allowlist convention: every entry is a
# deliberate, documented acceptance — not a blanket mute. `ignore-unfixed`
# is already on in docker.yml, so everything here HAS a fix available but
# is being consciously deferred with a stated reason.
#
# Review rule: anything reachable from the *runtime* attack surface gets
# upgraded, not ignored. The entries below are build-tooling transitives
# (tar / glob / minimatch / cross-spawn) that Next.js's standalone output
# trace still copies into the production runner image even though the served
# request handlers never invoke them. The CVEs are ReDoS / DoS / archive
# path-traversal that need attacker-controlled input reaching those libs'
# APIs — input the served app never feeds them.
#
# History: the frontend used to be a dev container, so this list also had to
# cover playwright/vitest/eslint etc. Those are GONE now — frontend/Dockerfile
# is a multi-stage production image (`next build` + standalone, no dev deps)
# and the runner stage strips the esbuild Go binary (2 CRITICAL + HIGH Go
# CVEs) outright. Only the standalone-traced transitives below remain, so this
# file stays — but it should never grow back to cover a dev toolchain.

# --- frontend dev-toolchain transitives (node_modules build tools) ---
# (rollup's CVE-2026-27606 is NOT listed here — it's actually fixed via a
# package.json `overrides` pin to rollup 3.30.0, not suppressed.)

# cross-spawn ReDoS — dev tooling path parsing, not request-path.
CVE-2024-21538

# glob CLI command injection — only via the glob binary's CLI, which we
# never invoke; it's a transitive lib dep of build tooling.
CVE-2025-64756

# minimatch ReDoS / unbounded-recursion DoS — glob-pattern matching in
# build tooling, fed static patterns, not attacker input.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# node-tar path-traversal / arbitrary-file-write on EXTRACTION. Fixes only
# exist in tar 7.x (major bump of an npm-internal transitive). We never
# extract untrusted archives at runtime — tar is pulled in by install-time
# tooling that unpacks our own trusted, lockfile-pinned packages.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
